  "worked_solution": "First, since $s=5t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{5}.$  \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{5}\\,i+(\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\frac{s}{5})j-4\\cdot \\frac{s}{5}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}s}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4s}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{5})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}s}{5})j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{5})k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
